Permanently delete a KG node AND all its edges. DESTRUCTIVE — prefer
kg_merge_nodes for duplicates (it preserves history instead of
destroying it).

Audited: requires a non-empty `reason`; refuses user-locked nodes and
nodes with user-locked edges; snapshots the node + every attached edge
into kg_revision_log so the deletion can be reverted; removes the
node's embeddings. Pass `dry_run: true` to preview the node + edge
count without committing.

Best practice: describe the node first to confirm it's the right one.
